  "per_asset_material_judgments": {
    "304b7": "Qualified in its complete3x3 caller and the full9x4 building strip at all native scales. The sparse dark vertical grille remains in the correct right-hand building bay, with the projecting lower block, adjacent gray panel and dark perimeter shadow coherent. Sharper frames have stronger relief; thin bars soften at native1 without becoming an extra opening.",
    "304b8": "Qualified in its complete3x3 caller and full strip. Exactly three short bars and one dark-red aperture remain recognizable, aligned below the existing damaged upper section and above the lower vented sill. The neighboring right cage and upper/lower projecting horizontal edges still meet their Source structure. Narrow tile/frame shading remains visible, with no new detached panel or aperture.",
    "304cf": "Qualified in its complete3x3 caller and the full9x5 red motif. The wide left cavity and asymmetric internal rails remain under the existing broken upper column segment. The bottom neighboring ruin keeps its separate short-cavity identity. Stronger gray chips and brighter fine red ground are visible, without displacing the narrow vertical building column.",
    "304d5": "Qualified in its complete3x3 caller and full motif. The pointed upper cavity, small central shelf and sparse dark interior remain distinct on the right column. The external gray rim, adjoining upper panel and lower ruin stay aligned; more regular bright chipped edges and fine ground contrast are limits.",
    "304d6": "Qualified in its complete3x3 caller and full motif. The low rubble cluster and hanging upper crosspiece retain a short ruined base below304cf, with the bottom border finishing the left column cleanly. Native1 is soft; larger scales reveal stronger relief and granular background. The base remains distinguishable from the taller neighboring cavities."
  },
